    <string name="help_connection_description">Explain connection modes</string>
    <string name="help_connection_title">Connection modes</string>
    <string name="help_connection_body">Direct USB and Direct Wi-Fi send PCM straight to the ASHA stack over TCP or UDP and bypass AudioTrack. UDP avoids TCP retransmission stalls; TCP protects packet order.\n\nThe three modes marked AudioTrack use Android audio routing and usually have more delay.\n\nDirect Bluetooth PAN is experimental: incoming PAN traffic and outgoing ASHA share the Bluetooth radio, so interruptions are more likely. Actual latency depends on the phone, hearing aids and network.</string>
    <string name="help_jitter_description">Explain jitter buffer</string>
    <string name="help_jitter_title">Jitter buffer</string>
    <string name="help_jitter_body">This setting applies only to the UDP modes marked AudioTrack. The Direct TCP and Direct UDP modes use the Direct buffer setting in the desktop sender.</string>
    <string name="setup_heading">Phone setup</string>
    <string name="setup_explanation">For Direct USB, connect the cable, enable USB tethering and USB debugging, authorize this PC in the Android prompt, and pair your hearing aids. The PC uses the IP and port shown above. For Wi-Fi or Bluetooth PAN, enable that connection on both devices. Allow Audio-Asha notifications.</string>
